what The three-door paper for REDS %807 recommends Door C, the document-start sentinel, and names its own falsifier in plain words: a count of the places that would have to learn about the sentinel, against the 12 place constructions Door B touches, with confidence stated as moderate because only one of the two costs carried a number. Nobody ran it. Measured before claiming rather than reasoned: the 12 does not reproduce under any counting rule I can state -- weave.rye holds SIX Place constructions, four place() accessors returning a four-field literal and two sentinel initializers in from_order_record and from_v2, and the tree-wide reading of every .run = literal across mantra/ is 47 with 34 of those inside witnesses rather than in the module. Door C's side has no number at all on that page, and the first reading is lopsided: module source outside the witnesses references lines.items 70 times, 58 in weave.rye, 10 in main.rye and 2 in diff.rye, and an implicit line held in the list is exactly what each of those readings would have to be classified against. So the falsifier looks answerable and the recommendation looks refutable, which is why the instrument classifies rather than totalling: a site comparing two sentinel-carrying weaves travels free, and a site comparing a count against a record's row count, a ceiling, or a diff length must learn about it, and only the second kind is a cost. THE PREDICTION IS WRITTEN HERE BEFORE THE RUN SO IT CAN BE WRONG OUT LOUD: Door C's must-learn count lands above Door B's whole accounting -- places, row types and record formats together -- and the elder page's recommendation flips to Door B. If instead the must-learn count lands at or under Door B's, Door C stands and this lap confirms a recommendation rather than turning it. One scan, one control, one witness, one roster row, one Field paper naming the reading. Takes NO ruling: which door the weave walks through stays Keaton's word, and this lap only puts a number beside each. Touches no module source, no ceiling any peer watches, no ledger row beyond %807's own reading, and no peer-claimed path; construction/standing-equipment.kyri is a one-row append that petrichor is also appending to this hour, named here so the rebase is expected rather than discovered.
